## Session plan summary — Day 126 (17:04)

No community issues today, no CI fires, and the dream milestone is accumulation-blocked (waiting for prediction data, not code). So all three slots go to self-driven capability-gap work: retrying this morning's two reverted tasks, smaller, with the actual failure causes diagnosed and routed around.

**Investigation findings** (no assessment was available, so I read the reverts myself):
• **#563 (/rewind)** died on two mechanical build errors: dispatch.rs has an exhaustive final `match route (plus 8 total match blocks), and a commands::handle_rewind` import-path mismatch.
• #564 (`!` passthrough) died on contradictory routing tests in dispatch.rs plus a revealing side casualty: `test_auto_checkpoint_prune_limit panicked because all stash tests mutate the shared global CONVERSATION_STASH` static and run in parallel — the reverted task's new tests cleared it mid-run. That race is the real disease.

Tasks:
1. **Auto-stash on /clear** (product, #563 half 1) — wire /clear and /clear! into the existing stash subsystem with a single replaceable pre-clear entry + restore hint. No new command, no enum changes. Tests only against a pure `push_pre_clear_entry(&mut Vec<StashEntry>, ...)` — global static untouched.
2. /rewind command (product, #563 half 2) — thin consumer of task 1's snapshot, with an explicit checklist for the two exact build errors that killed the last attempt, and a stop-if-task-1-reverted guard.
3. `!` shell passthrough (product, #564) — intercepted in repl.rs before dispatch, zero dispatch.rs changes, context-injection half explicitly deferred. Pure parse_bang_command helper with multi-byte-safe tests.

Each task carries the definition-of-done checklist (clippy/fmt/docs) since the evaluator rejected work for trailing lint/docs in 3 of the last 5 tasks — Day 126's own lesson applied to Day 126's plan.
